  "result": "Perfect! All 105 tests pass. I've successfully implemented VAT calculation:\n\n**src/invoices.js:**\n- Added `lineVat()` function that calculates VAT per line: `(line subtotal - line discount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100`\n- VAT is rounded per line using `roundCents()`\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n  - `vat` = sum of all line VATs (not a percentage of invoice total)\n  - `total` = `subtotal - discount + vat` (clamped at 0)\n\n**src/render.js:**\n- Shows \"VAT: +\" line only if VAT is non-zero\n- VAT line appears just above Total line\n- All amounts formatted with `formatEuros()`\n\n**Tests added (11 new):**\n- lineVat calculation with different rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n- VAT with and without discounts\n- VAT rendering in invoices\n- Correct total calculation with discount and VAT\n- Multiple VAT rates on same invoice\n- Clamping of amounts at 0\n\nThe implementation follows the decision that VAT is computed per line on the line's amount after discount, with each line's VAT rounded independently. The invoice VAT is then the sum of these rounded line VATs, never a percentage of the invoice total.",
